      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: pin repair worker base during validation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- pin one `origin/main` base snapshot for each repair Codex edit pass\n- stop edit workers from refetching, rebasing, and revalidating solely because `main` advances after validation\n- leave later movement to the existing deterministic final base sync and exact-head CI/review gates\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe repair prompt required Codex to always fetch latest `main` and keep iterating until merge-ready. On a fast-moving repository, a worker could pass `pnpm check:changed`, observe another base update, rebase, and restart the same validation repeatedly until its per-call timeout expired.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test dist/repair/fix-prompt-builder.test.js` (12 passed)\n- `pnpm run test:repair` (672 passed)\n- `pnpm run test:coverage:changed` (100% lines/functions, 89.17% branches)\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe complete local `pnpm run check` reached 780/782 unit tests; two unrelated workflow-helper tests require Bash 4 `${name,,}` syntax while macOS ships Bash 3.2. CI provides the Linux-shell proof for those tests.\n",
